1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,920
I figured out a way to help you get
the five million to pay off your debt.

2
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,960
PREVIOUSLY

3
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,000
Your mom is in gambling debt.

4
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,360
You don't have any evidence
that Mom stole it.

5
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:21,200
Then check the security cameras.

6
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,160
Where are you going, madam?

7
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,680
To watch the drama.

8
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,600
Chamoi really has to stick
her nose into everything.

9
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,440
I'll take the bags back for you, honey.

10
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,600
-I'll put everything away properly.
-Mom, don't.

11
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:49,840
You should go.

12
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,240
Where do you want me to go?

13
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,040
Anywhere. Go live your own life.

14
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,800
Do whatever you want.

15
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,320
If you want to gamble, go gamble.

16
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:08,840
If you want a new man, or however
many men you want, I won't stop you.

17
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:12,160
It's your life. You get to choose.

18
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,880
But they tricked me.

19
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,320
I'm telling the truth.

20
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:20,440
Liu was the one who set everything up.

21
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:24,160
You know she's been trying
to get us thrown out of this house.

22
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,480
And she was the one behind Pong too.

23
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,640
I don't care who was behind it.

24
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,400
What hurts me is that
you broke your promise.

25
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,480
You promised me

26
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,680
you were going to change

27
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,320
and become a better person.

28
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,720
You said you wouldn't
cause me any more trouble.

29
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,440
But you couldn't do it.

30
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,680
I made a mistake, sweetheart.

31
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,320
I was wrong.

32
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:56,160
Can you forgive me, Hathaya? I'm sorry.

33
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:59,600
How much longer am I supposed
to keep listening to your excuses?

34
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:06,000
I promise I'll change.

35
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,440
Take me to any temple and make me
swear an oath if you want.

36
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,360
-Please.
-Mom.

37
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,800
I want to be happy.

38
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:21,040
Can you give me my life back?

39
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:27,080
Ever since I was born,

40
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,400
I've been proud to be your daughter.

41
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,120
I've always tried to do the right thing.
I've tried to be a good person.

42
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:37,000
But you keep causing problems.

43
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,800
And I'm always the one
who has to fix them for you.

44
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,360
I don't even want to bring up

45
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:53,040
whose actions led to Grandma's death.

46
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,000
Forget it, Mom.

47
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:10,360
We can't go back and change the past.

48
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,200
I'm only going to look forward now.

49
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:20,280
I want to live my life.
I want to be happy.

50
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:23,480
I don't want to spend my life fixing
other people's problems anymore.

51
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,640
Please give me my life back.

52
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,360
Please, Mom.

53
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,320
All right.

54
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,360
I'll go.

55
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:01,720
But before I leave…

56
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:07,600
can I hug you one last time?

57
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,080
Do you know

58
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:33,000
who I love most?

59
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,080
Myself.

60
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,520
I've only ever thought about myself.

61
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:51,080
But I'm grateful

62
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:54,880
I was born as your grandma's daughter.

63
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,120
And the thing I'm proudest of…

64
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:07,000
is that I got to be your mother.

65
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,920
Now I understand
what you meant when you said

66
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,280
some only have parents
when it's convenient for them.

67
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:18,360
At least I've succeeded halfway.

68
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,080
Everything is spicy.

69
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,760
There isn't a single mild dish here.
How am I supposed to eat this?

70
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:30,560
-The maid is just--
-Forget it.

71
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:34,000
How many times have I told you
there has to be soup or something mild?

72
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,840
Why are you so stupid?

73
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,240
You never learn.

74
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,760
I was trying to tell you

75
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,120
that they were bringing
the soup and vegetables.

76
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,680
Why didn't you say so?

77
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,600
You wouldn't listen.

78
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,800
Are you talking back to me?

79
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,120
Talking back to me?

80
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,040
I'm sorry.

81
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,320
Remember this.

82
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:08,080
From now on, serve the mild dishes first.

83
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Do you understand?

84
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,880
Why do I have to teach you
something this simple?

85
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,160
Even the stupid maids
are smarter than you.

86
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,440
I'm sorry.

87
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:22,920
You eat first. I'll clean this up.

88
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,440
I'm not eating. I'm in no mood for it.

89
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,080
I'm going out to eat.

90
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:32,720
So slow. Hurry up.

91
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,640
Yeah?

92
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:37,360
You can't do anything right.
Stay away from me. You stink.

93
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,520
Look.

94
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,720
I'm telling you right now.

95
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:45,240
Go upstairs and clean everything up.

96
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,200
If I come back and it isn't spotless,

97
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,640
you'll regret it.

98
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,320
Open it.

99
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:01,920
Give me that. Close it.

100
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:29,680
Ramil.

101
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:32,280
Have you eaten yet?
I'll make you something.

102
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,400
What happened to your clothes?

103
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,480
I was careless earlier.

104
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:44,160
I was bringing the food out and tripped.
I spilled it all over myself.

105
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,720
If that were really what happened,

106
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,920
that man wouldn't have been
shouting all over the house.

107
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,040
Mom.

108
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,440
Stop protecting him.

109
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:59,800
Even though I don't live here anymore,
I know what he does to you.

110
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,760
Mom.

111
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,240
Come live with me.

112
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:14,720
You don't have to stay here as his servant
and let him treat you like this. Please.

113
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,880
I can't go.

114
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,480
Mom.

115
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,400
How long are you going
to let him hurt you?

116
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,680
Do you love him that much?

117
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,000
You can't leave him?

118
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:36,240
Mr. Saksit did so much for us.

119
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,920
If he hadn't helped us, I don't know
what our lives would have been like.

120
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:44,840
Mom, you've repaid him more than enough.

121
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,280
How much longer
are you going to endure this?

122
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,000
I don't know.

123
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,000
Maybe my whole life.

124
00:12:56,480 --> 00:13:00,160
Or until one of us dies. Maybe then
the debt of gratitude will be repaid.

125
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,440
I used to think

126
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,240
he was the one

127
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,080
keeping you chained here.

128
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,720
But he isn't.

129
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,200
You're the one

130
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:25,640
using that debt of gratitude
to imprison yourself.

131
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:29,960
Fine.

132
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:32,520
If you won't come with me,

133
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,760
then take care of yourself.

134
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,040
Ramil, where are you going?

135
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,640
Don't worry about me.

136
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:57,920
Take good care of yourself.
Look after your health.

137
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,040
I love you, Ramil.

138
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:26,360
Aunt Ann, you can take this out now.

139
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:29,440
Ramil.

140
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:32,120
I'll help carry it.

141
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:38,960
If you came to pick me up, you can
wait outside. I can serve it myself.

142
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,560
Did you forget? Today's a day off.

143
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:47,600
Then why are you here?

144
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,240
You want to know?

145
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,960
If you really want to know,

146
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:59,800
bring your ear closer.
I'll whisper it to you.

147
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:11,080
I don't want to know anymore.

148
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:15,720
Take this to Grandpa. It's almost time
for him to eat and take his medicine.

149
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,840
Go.

150
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:19,040
Go on.

151
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:21,600
-You really don't want to know?
-Go.

152
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:23,720
Fine.

153
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,760
Grandpa.

154
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:37,320
I'm sorry I haven't been around
to take care of you much lately.

155
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,400
I've been helping Raiwin with his work.

156
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:43,360
He has to thank the villagers,

157
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:46,360
and we've also been discussing
some good projects

158
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,920
that could support

159
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,200
our housing development.

160
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,640
That's wonderful, honey.

161
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,160
Not only are you a couple,

162
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:59,120
you're supporting
each other's businesses too.

163
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:02,960
Grandpa must be so proud of you.

164
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,840
Tell Raiwin to resign.

165
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,200
Politicians

166
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:16,280
are supposed to work for the community,
the people, and the country.

167
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:17,880
They're not supposed

168
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:20,360
to use the office to enrich themselves
and help their friends.

169
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:25,560
People like that aren't politicians.
They're businessmen.

170
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,360
Grandpa.

171
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:33,640
Politicians and business investors
need each other.

172
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,760
Raiwin became subdistrict chief

173
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:38,080
because I supported him.

174
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,200
It's time we got

175
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:43,400
a worthwhile return on our investment.

176
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,160
Everyone does it.

177
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:51,040
I'm an old man with a foot in the grave,

178
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:54,320
and Thai politics
still hasn't developed at all.

179
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:56,800
It hasn't moved forward.

180
00:16:57,720 --> 00:17:00,120
People say Thai dramas are trash.

181
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,040
But I don't think so.

182
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:05,359
Thai politics is far worse.

183
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:15,760
Why did the food take so long?

184
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:18,960
Were you waiting for us
to beg for our lives?

185
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:23,800
I'm not late. You came early.

186
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:24,880
You're just hangry.

187
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,400
The food is here.

188
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,240
This is yours, sir.

189
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,640
Is this even your job?

190
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:39,280
You're done now. Go.

191
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,160
What are you staring at?

192
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,200
Eat. It'll get cold.

193
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,560
Ramil, this isn't your place.

194
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,080
Didn't you hear what Mom said?

195
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:05,960
Hathaya.

196
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,640
You should teach your husband
some manners.

197
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,560
Ramil.

198
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:17,200
Go wait for me--

199
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,200
I invited Ramil to eat with us.

200
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:30,640
Father, I know you're pleased
with Ramil's work,

201
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,440
but I really don't think
this is appropriate.

202
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:37,720
I don't eat at the same table as workers.

203
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:44,160
If it makes you uncomfortable,

204
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,760
you and your daughter
can eat separately in the kitchen.

205
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:54,160
Hathaya.

206
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,200
After you finish eating,
prepare a room for Ramil.

207
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,080
What room, Grandpa?

208
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,840
Ramil is your husband.

209
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,840
It's time he moved in with you.

210
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,480
Father.

211
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:20,440
Father, you're going
to let Ramil live here?

212
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,600
You can't.

213
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:25,280
This man has a bad history. He once
tried to violate Hathaya in her room.

214
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,560
What if one day he loses control

215
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,960
and goes after Chayanee too?

216
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,280
From what I know of Ramil,

217
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,280
he isn't that kind of man.

218
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:42,120
But if it makes you uncomfortable,

219
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:43,760
I won't push it.

220
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:51,000
You and your daughter can move out
and live somewhere else.

221
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:58,000
If your things are too heavy,
I can help carry them.

222
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,120
No.

223
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,400
I'm staying here.

224
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,360
This is my house.

225
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,880
For you.

226
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,000
Why do you have to live here?

227
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:39,440
Grandpa said we're husband and wife.

228
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,640
We have to be together.

229
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:46,680
I don't believe that. I know you were
the one who asked Grandpa.

230
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,920
You know a lot, huh?

231
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,880
Chayanee and Liu

232
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,200
keep attacking you
and trying to get rid of you.

233
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,760
Look.

234
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,880
I'm worried about you.

235
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:03,040
So I'm looking after you.

236
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,040
This looks comfortable.

237
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:24,480
You can't. Get up.

238
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,520
-Why?
-We can't sleep together. Get up.

239
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:28,000
I don't want us sleeping together.

240
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:30,520
-We can sleep together. Why not?
-No, we can't.

241
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:32,440
-No.
-I don't mind.

242
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:34,120
I do.

243
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:03,880
You can sleep on the bed.

244
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:06,680
I'll put a mattress on the floor.

245
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:08,800
Come on.

246
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:11,800
Everyone knows we're husband and wife.

247
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:14,440
We can sleep together.
I don't mind. Come here.

248
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,240
Do you remember what you once told me?

249
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:24,360
You said you could never
love someone like me.

250
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:29,440
But thank you for coming here

251
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:32,400
to look after me as a coworker.

252
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,520
I'm going to get some things for you.

253
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:39,920
Wait--

254
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:46,800
Damn it. Why did I ever say that?

255
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:57,760
Raiwin, is your father home?

256
00:22:57,840 --> 00:22:59,800
I need to talk to him.

257
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,920
You should go home now.

258
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,120
Please.

259
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:07,720
Why? I'm here to talk about our wedding.

260
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,760
Today probably isn't a good time.

261
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,240
Go home. I'll call you later.

262
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,760
But we already agreed

263
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:18,720
that after the election,
we would get married.

264
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:21,040
Is your father going back on his word?

265
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,000
It's not like that.

266
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:27,600
Then I'm talking to him today.

267
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:29,960
Chayanee.

268
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:33,280
They're deliberately framing me.

269
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,520
They're trying to discredit me.

270
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:39,240
Damn it! What the hell is this?

271
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,720
Here's the coffee you asked for.

272
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,280
I don't want it.

273
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,280
I told you I'm in a bad mood.

274
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:49,640
Geez.

275
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,160
They're trying to discredit me.

276
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,000
Dad.

277
00:23:57,880 --> 00:24:01,200
I already told you I'm not seeing anyone.

278
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:02,520
Get them out of here.

279
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:05,600
You can't throw me out, Uncle.

280
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:08,360
I have something important
to discuss with you.

281
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:12,720
I'm sorry.

282
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:15,800
Can we talk another day?
Today really isn't convenient.

283
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:18,560
But today is convenient for me.
And I want to talk now.

284
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:25,480
Please listen to me. Go home now.

285
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,240
How about we go get
something to eat? Come on.

286
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:32,240
No. I don't want to spend time
with you today.

287
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:35,000
I want to settle this with your father.

288
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:37,360
Then say whatever you came to say
and get it over with.

289
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:40,600
I spent money helping
Raiwin win the election.

290
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:43,680
You promised me that if Raiwin
became subdistrict chief,

291
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:45,600
you'd ask Grandpa for my hand in marriage.

292
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:47,480
And it's been a long time already.

293
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:50,200
I've been busy. It hasn't been convenient.

294
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,320
Can we do it later?

295
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:52,720
I want to talk about it today.

296
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:54,120
What is your problem?

297
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:56,160
I've waited long enough.

298
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:59,440
And your son can't be trusted.
He keeps going after Hathaya.

299
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:01,480
That's why I hired those men to rape her.

300
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:03,600
It's just a shame they failed.

301
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,880
You hired men to rape Hathaya?

302
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:10,600
How could you do that?
She's your relative.

303
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:12,640
I've never considered her family.

304
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:15,240
Do you even realize what you've done?

305
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:18,520
Don't defend her.
And don't try to change the subject.

306
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:21,360
Today, you are going to ask Grandpa
for my hand.

307
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:24,280
I'm under investigation for old cases.

308
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:27,680
The streetlight case. The landfill case.
God knows what else.

309
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,160
I could go to prison.

310
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:33,080
How am I supposed to be in the mood
to arrange your wedding?

311
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:40,520
Uncle.

312
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:45,240
Will shouting like this
keep you out of prison?

313
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:52,160
Cases like this take money.

314
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:56,280
If you need money, ask Grandpa.

315
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:57,680
I'll help talk to him.

316
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:00,600
Why…

317
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,960
Why would your grandfather help me?

318
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:07,200
If Raiwin and I get married,

319
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:09,680
our two families will become one.

320
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:13,320
Grandpa will have to help his own family.

321
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,640
And the sooner I get married,

322
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:20,160
the sooner I'll have a chance of receiving

323
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,720
Grandpa's inheritance.

324
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:27,240
Raiwin.

325
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:31,280
We're going to Mr. Pichai's house.

326
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:33,200
Alright.

327
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,520
Well, former subdistrict chief.

328
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:10,400
I'll skip the formal greeting.

329
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,880
You don't like me anyway,

330
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:15,120
and I don't respect you.

331
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:16,160
Really?

332
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:19,760
Whether you greet me
properly or not, I don't care.

333
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:23,120
Ever since you left my house,

334
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:28,160
you've become a parasite
living off a woman here?

335
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:33,120
Living off a woman now, are you?

336
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,200
Ramil.

337
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:38,160
I live here because

338
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:42,760
Mr. Pichai asked me to help with the work
and to screen anyone coming in

339
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:45,800
so nothing inauspicious
gets into the house.

340
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:47,480
-That's too much--
-Dad.

341
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:53,640
Dad and I have business with Mr. Pichai.

342
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:56,680
I already told Grandpa we were coming.

343
00:27:57,320 --> 00:27:59,440
As for you,

344
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,200
go back to the workers' quarters.

345
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:03,720
Hathaya.

346
00:28:03,800 --> 00:28:07,560
Take your worker husband
back to your area.

347
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:09,560
Don't let him bark at the guests.

348
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:13,280
And if you can't train him
and he keeps barking,

349
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,680
get a muzzle

350
00:28:15,760 --> 00:28:17,440
and chain him up.

351
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,480
We told you to leave, so go.

352
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:26,840
Both of you. I can't stand
looking at your faces.

353
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:29,760
If you made an appointment with Grandpa,

354
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:32,120
you'll have to put up
with looking at our faces.

355
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:34,080
Grandpa told Ramil and me
to take care of you.

356
00:28:40,280 --> 00:28:43,680
Well? What do you say, former
subdistrict chief? What should we do?

357
00:28:49,680 --> 00:28:50,800
Ramil.

358
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:55,320
Please let Mr. Pichai know
my father has arrived.

359
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:59,280
Since becoming subdistrict chief,

360
00:28:59,800 --> 00:29:01,280
you've become much more polite.

361
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:03,800
Fine.

362
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,280
Come on.

363
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,840
Please be patient, Mr. Saksit.

364
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:17,440
It won't be long before
Chayanee marries Raiwin.

365
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:21,000
Once that happens, we'll throw him out.

366
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:26,960
Please come in. Father is waiting.

367
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:28,160
-Thank you.
-Wow.

368
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:30,880
What beautiful flowers.

369
00:29:33,120 --> 00:29:34,760
Father is waiting.

370
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:36,560
Come on.

371
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:39,000
Please.

372
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,440
-Hello, Mr. Pichai.
-Hello.

373
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:41,360
Here.

374
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:42,720
For you, sir.

375
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:44,440
-Thank you.
-Hello.

376
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:48,480
Mr. Saksit.

377
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:51,880
You can get to the point.
I don't have much time.

378
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:54,240
It'll soon be time for me
to eat and take my medicine.

379
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:56,400
I've come to formally

380
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:59,360
ask for Chayanee's hand in marriage

381
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:01,120
for my son Raiwin.

382
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:09,000
What do you think, Father?
I have no objection.

383
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:13,080
Raiwin is a good man. He has a good career

384
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:15,800
and comes from a good family.

385
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:22,000
A person's career and family status
are only secondary.

386
00:30:22,080 --> 00:30:23,880
What matters most

387
00:30:25,640 --> 00:30:27,840
is character and whether
two people can live together.

388
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:32,320
What do you think of Raiwin?

389
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:40,120
Raiwin has never

390
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,280
disappointed me or made me sad.

391
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:47,680
Whenever I'm with him, I feel safe.

392
00:30:47,760 --> 00:30:51,080
We complete each other, Grandpa.

393
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:56,720
If you've made up your mind,
I won't object.

394
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,600
Okay.

395
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:00,400
Thank you very much, Mr. Pichai.

396
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:01,600
I'll start

397
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:04,920
preparing the wedding and find
an auspicious date as soon as possible.

398
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:08,480
If that's everything, I'm going to rest.

399
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:13,760
Grandpa.

400
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:16,680
Mr. Saksit served

401
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:21,680
as subdistrict chief honestly
and sincerely for our community.

402
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:28,040
You said this concerns Mr. Saksit,

403
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:31,480
so he should be the one to speak.

404
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:38,840
Well, Mr. Pichai,

405
00:31:39,360 --> 00:31:42,280
I'm being politically persecuted.

406
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:45,360
The people who lost to Raiwin

407
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,480
filed complaints accusing me

408
00:31:47,560 --> 00:31:50,640
of corruption involving various
Subdistrict Office projects.

409
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:54,560
So I was hoping you could support me

410
00:31:57,400 --> 00:31:58,640
with around

411
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:02,920
ten million baht. I could use the money
to take care of the cases.

412
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:04,640
Well…

413
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:07,760
But I promise you, Mr. Pichai,

414
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:13,160
the return you'll receive will be worth
far more than ten million.

415
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:15,760
I'll have Raiwin

416
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:18,520
approve a new road project

417
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:21,400
that runs through your land.

418
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,760
A road through my land?

419
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:36,360
That could increase its value
tenfold or twentyfold.

420
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:40,320
Thank you very much.

421
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:42,760
Thank you, Mr. Pichai,

422
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:45,120
for supporting me.

423
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:48,360
But I still have three questions.

424
00:32:50,200 --> 00:32:51,480
First.

425
00:32:53,040 --> 00:32:55,520
Can money really make
a corruption case go away?

426
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:02,600
Mr. Pichai.

427
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:07,400
Money can settle cases.
I've done it before.

428
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:12,280
Second. If the road goes through my land,

429
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:15,000
what do the people get out of it?

430
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:19,640
If the road goes through your land,

431
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:21,440
the locals don't get anything.

432
00:33:21,520 --> 00:33:23,440
You do.

433
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:26,480
But I already had Raiwin
prepare other projects.

434
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:28,960
An anti-drug sports initiative.

435
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:32,800
Distributing goods to poor families.

436
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:36,680
Projects like that will definitely
benefit the villagers.

437
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,000
Third.

438
00:33:41,760 --> 00:33:43,600
Is Raiwin chief,
or are you still in charge?

439
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:46,840
Of course Raiwin is.

440
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:49,400
Young people

441
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,520
are popular these days,

442
00:33:51,600 --> 00:33:53,840
so Raiwin

443
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:57,000
has to be the face, but I still

444
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:58,760
handle the administration.

445
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:03,680
Then Raiwin is just your puppet?

446
00:34:08,719 --> 00:34:11,440
From all three of your answers,

447
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:14,120
I still don't see anything
you're doing for the people.

448
00:34:14,639 --> 00:34:16,000
All I see is what benefits you

449
00:34:18,400 --> 00:34:19,480
and your friends.

450
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:25,400
And one more thing. I don't support
passing power down like this.

451
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:31,120
The era of old dinosaurs like you is over.

452
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:36,400
What exactly do you want?

453
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:41,239
I wasted my time coming here
just to be insulted.

454
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:43,520
Are you going to help me or not?

455
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:51,600
I'm one of the locals.

456
00:34:52,239 --> 00:34:55,440
I want politicians
who work for people like me.

457
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:01,760
If you're not ready
to be good politicians,

458
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,040
then resign.

459
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,920
Don't become political parasites.

460
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:13,280
Ramil. Take me to rest.

461
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:14,440
-Yes, sir.
-Raiwin.

462
00:35:15,160 --> 00:35:16,000
We're leaving.

463
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:22,680
Chayanee.

464
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:27,000
Uncle. Uncle.

465
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:33,000
Uncle.

466
00:35:33,880 --> 00:35:37,000
Uncle. Please calm down.

467
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:38,840
Calm down?

468
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:42,600
I'm facing criminal charges
and you want me to calm down?

469
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:44,920
You said if we discussed the wedding,

470
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,800
your grandfather

471
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:50,040
would treat me like family and help me.

472
00:35:50,120 --> 00:35:52,600
And what happened? What was that?

473
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:55,400
Your grandfather

474
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:59,040
tore me apart. What the hell was that?

475
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:02,000
Grandpa is--

476
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:05,080
He's old-fashioned.
He clings to all those ridiculous ideals.

477
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,560
I'll

478
00:36:06,640 --> 00:36:10,400
talk to him again and try to persuade him.

479
00:36:10,920 --> 00:36:13,280
Grandpa has probably been manipulated

480
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,360
by Ramil and Hathaya.

481
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:16,640
For now, Mr. Saksit,

482
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:20,120
start preparing the dowry. Chayanee and I

483
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:22,520
will find a way to help you.

484
00:36:22,600 --> 00:36:23,600
Okay?

485
00:36:28,640 --> 00:36:30,160
If Mr. Pichai

486
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:32,360
won't help me,

487
00:36:35,320 --> 00:36:37,080
then forget joining our families.

488
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:42,440
There will be no wedding.

489
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:47,120
No. My daughter's reputation
will be ruined.

490
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:48,200
Oh my God.

491
00:36:48,960 --> 00:36:49,800
Raiwin.

492
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:54,120
You can't abandon me.
I've helped you so much.

493
00:36:57,280 --> 00:36:58,960
You know I can't do anything about this.

494
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:01,760
My father decides everything.

495
00:37:03,080 --> 00:37:04,160
We'll talk later.

496
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:07,640
No. There has to be a wedding.

497
00:37:08,240 --> 00:37:11,720
Chayanee, calm down. Lower your voice.

498
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:15,040
I won't accept this, Mom.
Raiwin can't leave me.

499
00:37:15,120 --> 00:37:16,480
Calm down, sweetheart.

500
00:37:16,560 --> 00:37:18,080
Dad.

501
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:22,000
I'll try talking to Chayanee and ask
for another meeting with Mr. Pichai.

502
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:23,840
Don't.

503
00:37:23,920 --> 00:37:26,600
I'll put together a concrete proposal

504
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,840
and write out the benefits
Mr. Pichai would receive.

505
00:37:30,600 --> 00:37:32,400
I think he might change his mind.

506
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:35,240
I told you not to bother.

507
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:39,240
That Pichai is dumber than the ancient
dinosaurs he keeps rambling about.

508
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:42,000
He clings to all these idiotic ideals.

509
00:37:42,080 --> 00:37:46,680
I offered him a project
that could make him a billionaire.

510
00:37:46,760 --> 00:37:49,160
Stuff money in his coffin,
he still won't care.

511
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:51,520
I'm trying to help you.

512
00:37:52,200 --> 00:37:53,520
What do you want me to do?

513
00:37:54,120 --> 00:37:55,240
What do I want you to do?

514
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:57,480
You.

515
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:59,120
Break up with Chayanee.

516
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:02,040
She probably won't accept that.

517
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:06,280
You're a man.

518
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:14,080
Don't let a woman
lead you around by the nose!

519
00:38:14,160 --> 00:38:16,280
You're a man, not a buffalo.

520
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:19,520
I've never let a woman push me around.

521
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:21,320
We control them.

522
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:24,440
If Chayanee can't help us anymore,

523
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:25,920
then break up with her.

524
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:30,320
I'll find you a woman who's better
and more capable myself.

525
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:34,640
Can't you let me think
and handle my own life for once?

526
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:37,600
Think?

527
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:40,240
You're too stupid to think for yourself.

528
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:44,680
Why is Ramil doing so well now?
Because of Pichai.

529
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:47,160
Pichai loves him and trusts him.

530
00:38:47,240 --> 00:38:50,840
If that old man dies
and Hathaya inherits everything,

531
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:52,440
do you understand what that means?

532
00:38:52,520 --> 00:38:54,440
Ramil will end up
even better off than you.

533
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:57,080
And worst of all,
he'll stand over your head.

534
00:38:57,160 --> 00:38:59,320
He'll spit down on you.

535
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:01,000
Do you know

536
00:39:02,040 --> 00:39:03,360
why that old Pichai

537
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,600
refused to help me? Because of Ramil.

538
00:39:05,680 --> 00:39:08,160
He keeps turning Pichai against us.

539
00:39:08,240 --> 00:39:10,120
Damn it. Idiot.

540
00:39:14,720 --> 00:39:16,920
Go. Why are you still standing there?

541
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:18,200
‎Go.

542
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,040
Nothing ever goes the way I want.

543
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,280
Did you get what I asked for?

544
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:41,520
Why is there so little?
There should be more than this.

545
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,640
This is really all I have left.

546
00:39:44,720 --> 00:39:46,960
How can this be all that's left?

547
00:39:47,040 --> 00:39:49,800
I bought you jewelry to wear to events.

548
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:53,240
You already made me sell it
when you were campaigning.

549
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:54,880
You spent all that money.

550
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:58,200
What the hell?

551
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:01,600
Do you understand how much money
I need to settle these cases?

552
00:40:01,680 --> 00:40:03,880
Get it?

553
00:40:09,160 --> 00:40:10,960
The ring. Take it off.

554
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:18,280
That's Anon's, right?

555
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:21,120
You love him that much?

556
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:23,000
You won't take it off?

557
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:25,560
It's my wedding ring.
I want to keep it for Ramil.

558
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:27,000
No. Take it off.

559
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:29,520
-No.
-Take it off.

560
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:31,120
-It's the only thing I--
-Give me.

561
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:33,840
-Give it to me.
-Please let me keep it.

562
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:35,000
No.

563
00:40:35,080 --> 00:40:37,360
Don't take it.
I want to save it for Ramil.

564
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:39,360
Do you? I won't let you.

565
00:40:39,440 --> 00:40:40,280
Give it here.

566
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:44,520
Please let me keep it.

567
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:46,520
Nothing belongs to you.

568
00:40:46,600 --> 00:40:48,120
Not even you.

569
00:40:48,640 --> 00:40:51,600
You belong to me. Remember that.

570
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:55,880
No. Don't take it. Please.

571
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:57,960
You're begging?

572
00:40:58,040 --> 00:40:59,560
Please.

573
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:03,800
Mr. Saksit, have you ever loved me at all?

574
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,800
I brought your money.

575
00:41:26,160 --> 00:41:27,000
Paying me back?

576
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:31,280
How much do you want this time?

577
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:35,600
I'm only here to repay you.

578
00:41:38,200 --> 00:41:40,480
I invested that money with a friend.

579
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:42,320
Things are going well now.

580
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:45,280
I wish I could repay you more,

581
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:48,360
but we're only just getting started.

582
00:41:49,200 --> 00:41:51,160
I'm sorry it took me so long.

583
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:56,360
I won't take up any more of your time.

584
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,800
I know you don't want to see me.

585
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:05,000
I'll go.

586
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:22,760
Your father kept his word.

587
00:42:23,280 --> 00:42:25,320
Can you forgive him now?

588
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:35,800
Even if he pays back
a thousand times more,

589
00:42:39,120 --> 00:42:40,720
money can't buy our happiness back.

590
00:42:49,720 --> 00:42:51,360
Whose car is that?

591
00:42:51,440 --> 00:42:53,120
Ms. Sanguansri has a visitor.

592
00:42:54,040 --> 00:42:56,280
-Who?
-Mr. Anon.

593
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:06,880
What do you need?

594
00:43:06,960 --> 00:43:10,080
You could've called to meet somewhere.
I don't want you here.

595
00:43:11,560 --> 00:43:13,920
I needed to see you
about something important.

596
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:16,960
The business I started
with my friend is doing well.

597
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:21,880
I'm happy for you.
But if that's all, you should go.

598
00:43:24,160 --> 00:43:25,680
I understand.

599
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:29,200
If Mr. Saksit sees me here,
he won't be happy.

600
00:43:35,680 --> 00:43:36,640
Here.

601
00:43:37,360 --> 00:43:38,560
I brought the money back.

602
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:39,960
TEN MILLION

603
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:44,880
I'm trying to make everything better.

604
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:48,840
I want you and our son
to have a good life.

605
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,920
And I've always felt guilty

606
00:43:55,720 --> 00:43:57,520
and ashamed

607
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:00,400
for abandoning you both.

608
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:08,080
Thank you so much for returning the money.

609
00:44:08,840 --> 00:44:12,320
Ramil intended to use it to build a house.

610
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:15,680
He's always dreamed
of having a home of his own.

611
00:44:21,920 --> 00:44:24,080
I may never get the chance
to be a good husband.

612
00:44:26,080 --> 00:44:28,520
But I want to be a good father to our son.

613
00:44:30,840 --> 00:44:32,880
And I'll bring more money
for you and Ramil.

614
00:44:39,960 --> 00:44:41,160
Sanguansri.

615
00:44:42,520 --> 00:44:43,880
What happened to your face?

616
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:50,360
Nothing. I fell.

617
00:44:50,880 --> 00:44:52,160
If that's all, please go.

618
00:45:07,840 --> 00:45:09,440
Thank you for taking the time

619
00:45:09,520 --> 00:45:11,760
to have coffee with me, Ingorn.

620
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:15,160
I should be thanking you, Chief.

621
00:45:15,240 --> 00:45:18,120
I know how busy you are.

622
00:45:19,440 --> 00:45:22,440
No matter how busy I am,
I can always make time for you.

623
00:45:24,680 --> 00:45:25,920
Today,

624
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:29,800
I also have a good project
to present to you.

625
00:45:33,440 --> 00:45:35,440
If I build a road through here,

626
00:45:35,520 --> 00:45:37,080
the value of this land

627
00:45:37,600 --> 00:45:39,680
will increase several times over.

628
00:45:41,120 --> 00:45:43,000
I'll also make sure

629
00:45:43,080 --> 00:45:45,960
the electricity and water systems
are fully developed.

630
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:48,800
What do you think?

631
00:45:49,840 --> 00:45:52,440
Chief, you're being so good to me.

632
00:45:53,520 --> 00:45:55,320
How am I supposed to repay you?

633
00:45:59,880 --> 00:46:01,200
You don't need to repay me.

634
00:46:04,160 --> 00:46:07,160
As long as we cooperate,
everything will work out.

635
00:46:15,640 --> 00:46:17,560
If you keep treating me like this,

636
00:46:18,080 --> 00:46:20,560
won't your girlfriend tear me apart?

637
00:46:22,360 --> 00:46:23,360
No, she won't.

638
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:31,720
-Your drinks.
-I'll serve it.

639
00:46:34,920 --> 00:46:37,320
Hey. What are you doing?

640
00:46:38,800 --> 00:46:42,200
I'm the one who should
be asking what you're doing.

641
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,920
I'm discussing business with Raiwin.
What does that have to do with you?

642
00:46:46,520 --> 00:46:49,920
What's that got to do with me?
You can say that with a straight face?

643
00:46:50,440 --> 00:46:53,960
Raiwin is my boyfriend. Everyone
in the restaurant knows he's my boyfriend.

644
00:46:56,280 --> 00:46:59,000
Raiwin, I'm leaving.

645
00:47:00,360 --> 00:47:01,560
Come on. I'll take you.

646
00:47:04,200 --> 00:47:05,200
Chayanee.

647
00:47:05,280 --> 00:47:08,680
Thanks for remembering my name.

648
00:47:08,760 --> 00:47:12,000
Now burn this into your skull too.

649
00:47:12,080 --> 00:47:13,440
Raiwin is mine.

650
00:47:13,520 --> 00:47:16,080
Stay away from my man.

651
00:47:16,160 --> 00:47:17,680
That's enough.

652
00:47:18,200 --> 00:47:20,640
I'm reporting you to the police.
I'll press charges.

653
00:47:20,720 --> 00:47:22,840
Go ahead. I can afford it.

654
00:47:24,040 --> 00:47:25,480
Charge me by the slap.

655
00:47:28,120 --> 00:47:29,720
You think you're the only one with money?

656
00:47:29,800 --> 00:47:32,920
You slapped me?
You just declared war on me.

657
00:47:37,200 --> 00:47:38,320
Enough.

658
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:40,000
Both of you.

659
00:47:40,080 --> 00:47:41,000
Stop.

660
00:47:41,520 --> 00:47:42,480
Raiwin.

661
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:43,800
Enough.

662
00:47:45,160 --> 00:47:47,200
Come on. I'll walk you out.

663
00:47:52,240 --> 00:47:53,600
You damaged the restaurant.

664
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:55,160
You have to pay for it,

665
00:47:55,240 --> 00:47:57,360
or I'll call the police.

666
00:48:02,520 --> 00:48:05,200
Even if I destroyed the entire restaurant,
I could afford it.

667
00:48:05,720 --> 00:48:07,360
Remember that. I'm rich.

668
00:48:09,120 --> 00:48:11,160
I'm really sorry, Ingorn.

669
00:48:11,680 --> 00:48:13,080
Go take care of your girlfriend.

670
00:48:13,160 --> 00:48:16,480
Ingorn, I'm really sorry.

671
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:20,000
There's nothing between
Chayanee and me anymore.

672
00:48:20,080 --> 00:48:21,560
I apologize again.

673
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:25,680
And please keep my project in mind.

674
00:48:26,440 --> 00:48:27,480
Please.

675
00:48:30,200 --> 00:48:32,160
You shameless bitch. You're educated.

676
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:35,080
Can't you find your own husband?
Do you have to steal someone else's?

677
00:48:35,600 --> 00:48:38,640
Come back and slap me again.
Then you'll know I fight back.

678
00:48:38,720 --> 00:48:39,560
Come back.

679
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:41,800
Enough.

680
00:48:46,120 --> 00:48:49,120
Instead of taking my side,
you're protecting her.

681
00:48:49,200 --> 00:48:50,240
Stop acting crazy.

682
00:48:50,320 --> 00:48:51,720
I'm crazy because of you.

683
00:48:51,800 --> 00:48:54,280
I warned you. If you break up with me,

684
00:48:54,360 --> 00:48:55,280
you're going to regret it.

685
00:48:55,360 --> 00:48:56,600
What the hell do you expect?

686
00:48:56,680 --> 00:48:58,040
You promised

687
00:48:58,120 --> 00:49:00,160
Grandpa would help my father.

688
00:49:00,920 --> 00:49:02,440
You couldn't make it happen.

689
00:49:03,840 --> 00:49:05,720
My father is pressuring me too.

690
00:49:06,480 --> 00:49:08,240
You can do whatever you want,

691
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,000
but you are not getting another woman.

692
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:16,680
If you don't want me seeing someone else,

693
00:49:18,920 --> 00:49:20,320
then find the money for me.

694
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:29,440
What do you mean by that?

695
00:49:30,160 --> 00:49:33,400
If I can't find the money
to help your father settle his case,

696
00:49:33,920 --> 00:49:35,680
you're going to find another woman?

697
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:37,840
Answer me.

698
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:56,720
Raiwin threatened to break up with me.

699
00:49:56,800 --> 00:49:58,760
Where else am I supposed
to find the money?

700
00:49:58,840 --> 00:50:00,240
I came to give you the money.

701
00:50:00,320 --> 00:50:02,960
And I had no idea Pong
was going to show up.

702
00:50:03,040 --> 00:50:06,320
If Grandpa dies, his inheritance

703
00:50:06,400 --> 00:50:08,680
will go to you.

704
00:50:08,760 --> 00:50:11,280
If Grandpa won't give it to me,
then I won't ask.

705
00:50:11,360 --> 00:50:12,640
I'll steal it.

706
00:50:12,720 --> 00:50:14,440
All this time, I let you
take care of Grandpa.

707
00:50:14,520 --> 00:50:16,680
But you almost got him killed.

708
00:52:11,040 --> 00:52:12,960
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
